{
  "kanda": "kishkindha",
  "sarga": 63,
  "title": "Sampaati gets new wings and flew away",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga63/kishkindhasans63.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga63/kishkindhaitrans63.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Sampaati regains his wings when he passes information to the monkeys. Sampaati flies away for flight-test of his newborn wings wishing the monkeys success. Then the enthused monkeys journey on to southern direction, as directed by Sampaati."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये किष्किन्ध काण्डे त्रि षष्टितमः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 63rd chapter in Kishkindha Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "4.63.1",
      "label": "4.63.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "एतैः अन्यैः च बहुभिः वाक्यैः वाक्य विशारदः |\nमाम् प्रशस्य अभ्यनुज्ञाप्य प्रविष्टः स स्वम् आलयम्",
      "iast": "etaiḥ anyaiḥ ca bahubhiḥ vākyaiḥ vākya viśāradaḥ |\nmām praśasya abhyanujñāpya praviṣṭaḥ sa svam ālayam",
